# A switch of macOS' appearance (Automatic at sunset, or View ▸ Appearance) recolours the sidebar, the
# window's backdrop and the empty card in one main-thread turn, so no frame shows half the old look.
# systemAppearance=…&themeShown=… reads them back in the turn of the switch, before anything deferred
# runs. Until 0.1.55 the backdrop and sidebar waited a main-queue hop behind the card.
# Pastel (#FFCBD1, empty-card-appearance.scenario's) is on Auto with one set of colours, which keep their
# light look on Dark (#171): its theme, shell and sidebar read light on both sides, and what the switch
# changes is the material under the sidebar and the empty card's veil (CardVeil.noTabCard: 0.65 on
# Light, its 0.35 cap on Dark). Dusk (auto-theme.scenario's) is on Auto with a dark half, so its theme,
# window content and sidebar themselves turn dark and back. The first launch's own Personal space is
# fixed Dark and would never switch.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
